 - **Routing (`routing`, per model `model_routing`).** `sort` `price` (default) | `throughput` | `latency`; `min_quantization` (default `fp8`; an endpoint below it or with an unknown quantization is not used; `any` turns the filter off); `data_collection` `deny` (default) | `allow`; `zdr` (default false); `min_uptime_pct` (default 95, the lower of the endpoint's 30-minute and 1-day uptime); `ignore` and `order` (provider slugs). The cheapest endpoints are often fp4, hence the fp8 default; on 2026-11-04 `moonshotai/kimi-k3.1-pro` had no endpoint at fp8 or better (only fp4/mxfp4/unknown), so it needs a `model_routing` override or every job on it is refused at start.
 - **How routing is applied.** Claude Code sends no OpenRouter `provider` object. The `:floor` / `:nitro` model variants only choose a sort (price / throughput) and widen the pool with flex / priority tiers, and the account preferences (privacy settings) cover data policy and ignored providers account-wide, with no quantization and nothing per job ([provider selection](https://openrouter.ai/docs/guides/routing/provider-selection), [floor](https://openrouter.ai/docs/guides/routing/model-variants/floor)). OpenRouter's Anthropic-compatible `POST /api/v1/messages` does accept a `provider` object (`MessagesRequest.provider` in its [OpenAPI spec](https://openrouter.ai/docs/openapi/openapi.yaml)). So the wrapper runs a **loopback proxy per job** (127.0.0.1, a kernel-picked port, closed when claude exits): claude gets `ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL` = the proxy and a random per-job `ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN`; the proxy checks that token, sets the request's `model` to the slug and its `provider` object to the policy (`sort`, `quantizations`, `data_collection`, `zdr`, `ignore` plus the endpoints below the uptime floor, `order` = the policy's order followed by the eligible endpoints ranked cheapest first, fallbacks allowed inside those filters), adds `session_id` (OpenRouter's sticky routing, so the prompt cache stays warm), and forwards it with the real key. The ranking reads the public endpoints list (`/api/v1/models/<slug>/endpoints`, no key) when the job starts; `stderr.log` names the endpoint the policy picks.
